<h2 id=3D"ePartsProductSpecificationDocument-1.Purpose"><strong>1. Purpose<=
/strong></h2>
<p>The eParts Services Data Strategy aims to establish a modern, secure, po=
rtable [QA-PORT], performant, and cost-effective data platform. This platfo=
rm will consolidate data from various sources (initially including those ho=
sted on Microsoft Azure [CON-03]), enabling data processing, advanced analy=
tics, enhanced reporting capabilities, MLOps readiness, and secure data acc=
ess for internal eParts users, tenants (customers), and potentially partner=
s. The platform will provide MLOps readiness, a managed model registry and =
promotion workflow, a versioned online/offline feature store, experiment tr=
acking, secure inference/serving endpoints, telemetry for live model perfor=
mance &amp; drift, provisioning for model updates (e.g., canary/blue-green)=
, and a new tenant-scoped API to support MLOps.</p>
<p>The key objectives are to replace legacy reporting systems, improve data=
 accessibility and searchability, enable reproducible and governed ML, ensu=
re robust data governance [CON-01] supporting granular access needs identif=
ied in personas (e.g., PS1-PS13), support integration with BI tools [CAP-DA=
Q-03], enhance operational efficiency while managing costs effectively [CON=
-02], and minimize vendor lock-in [QA-PORT].</p>
<h2 id=3D"ePartsProductSpecificationDocument-2.Operators">2. Operators</h2>
<p>The primary operators of the eParts Data Strategy platform will include:=
</p>
<p style=3D"margin-left: 30.0px;"><strong>2.1. eParts Developers:</strong> =
Responsible for building, extending, and maintaining the platform's compone=
nts, including ingestion pipelines, APIs, and reporting tools. (See Persona=
s: PS3, PS4)</p>
<p style=3D"margin-left: 30.0px;"><strong>2.2. eParts MLOps/Data Science Te=
am:</strong> Responsible for developing, deploying, and managing machine le=
arning models and the associated infrastructure [CAP-ML-01, CAP-ML-02]. Own=
s the model registry, experiment tracking, feature store, model serving, an=
d performance telemetry.</p>
<p style=3D"margin-left: 30.0px;"><strong>2.3. eParts IT/Infrastructure Tea=
m:</strong> Responsible for managing the underlying cloud infrastructure (A=
zure), monitoring system health, and ensuring security and availability [QA=
-SEC].</p>
<p style=3D"margin-left: 30.0px;"><strong>2.4. Tenant Administrators:</stro=
ng> Will have operational roles related to managing their specific users or=
 accessing certain platform features, governed by RBAC [QA-SEC-01], [CAP-DS=
M-05]. (See Personas: PS8, PS9)</p>
<p style=3D"margin-left: 30.0px;"><strong>2.5 Customers of tenants: </stron=
g>Customers buying from various tenants who are interested in seeing their =
spending and order metrics through dashboards.</p>
<h2 id=3D"ePartsProductSpecificationDocument-3.Personas"><strong>3. Persona=
s</strong></h2>
<p>Please refer to the <a href=3D"https://epartsservices.atlassian.net/wiki=
/x/FgC-F" rel=3D"nofollow">Personas</a>.</p>
<h2 id=3D"ePartsProductSpecificationDocument-4.ProductDescription"><strong>=
4. Product Description</strong></h2>
<p>Please refer to the <a href=3D"https://epartsservices.atlassian.net/wiki=
/x/G4C4F" rel=3D"nofollow">Product Description</a> for in depth product des=
cription.</p>
<p>The eParts Data Strategy Platform is envisioned as a cloud-native data p=
latform solution, designed with <a href=3D"https://epartsservices.atlassian=
.net/wiki/spaces/CMU2026/pages/818610219/eParts+Product+Specification+Docum=
ent#7.-Quality-Attributes-(Non-Functional-Requirements)" rel=3D"nofollow">v=
arious quality attributes</a> in mind. It will ingest data from diverse sou=
rces including relational databases (SQL Server transitioning to Azure SQL/=
Managed Instance) [CAP-DI-01, CON-03], file stores (Azure Blob Storage, SFT=
P) [CAP-DI-02, CON-03], real-time feeds (UPS) [CAP-DI-03], and logs [CAP-DI=
-04].</p>
<h3 id=3D"ePartsProductSpecificationDocument-4.1.ConceptualModel"><strong>4=
.1. Conceptual Model</strong></h3>
<p>The platform will feature:</p>
<p style=3D"margin-left: 30.0px;"><strong>4.1.1. Configurable data ingestio=
n pipelines</strong> supporting batch and near real-time processing (levera=
ging CDC) [CAP-DI-05, CAP-DI-06, CAP-DI-07], including data transformation =
[CAP-DI-09].</p>
<p style=3D"margin-left: 30.0px;"><strong>4.1.2. A centralized cloud-based =
data repository</strong> A centralized cloud-based data repository [CAP-DSM=
-01] supporting structured and unstructured data, ensuring logical tenant d=
ata isolation and potentially customer-level scoping within tenants [CAP-DS=
M-05].</p>
<p style=3D"margin-left: 30.0px;"><strong>4.1.3. Robust data governance enf=
orced via Auth0 integration</strong> Robust data governance enforced via Au=
th0 integration [CON-01], including multi-level RBAC [QA-SEC-01], user acti=
vity tracking [CAP-DSM-06], data deletion capabilities [CAP-DSM-04, CON-06]=
, and data warehouse permissions (wherever required).</p>
<p style=3D"margin-left: 30.0px;"><strong>4.1.4. Data access layers providi=
ng APIs </strong>for internal applications, tenant/partner BI tools [CAP-DA=
Q-02, CAP-DAQ-03], and ad-hoc querying [CAP-DAQ-01], designed using standar=
d protocols where feasible to enhance portability [QA-PORT].</p>
<p style=3D"margin-left: 30.0px;"><strong>4.1.5. An enhanced reporting syst=
em </strong>with template creation, customization, ad-hoc capabilities [CAP=
-RA-01, CAP-RA-02, CAP-RA-03, CAP-RA-05], saved queries [CAP-RA-08], schedu=
led delivery [CAP-RA-06], and CSV export [CAP-RA-09].</p>
<p style=3D"margin-left: 30.0px;"><strong>4.1.6. A dashboarding system </st=
rong>which would show historical and real-time data suited to the needs of =
the individuals using it. [CAP-RA-01].</p>
<p style=3D"margin-left: 30.0px;"><strong>4.1.7. Infrastructure [CAP-ML-01]=
, tooling [CAP-ML-02], and data access </strong>to support the ML lifecycle=
<strong> </strong>for use cases like shipping estimation, vendor rating, an=
omaly detection, and inventory management.</p>
<p style=3D"margin-left: 30.0px;"><strong>4.1.8. MLOps readiness services</=
strong>: Managed model registry, feature store, experiment tracking, infere=
nce/serving endpoints, and live telemetry for model performance &amp; drift=
.</p>
<p style=3D"margin-left: 30.0px;"><strong>4.1.9. Mechanisms for automated b=
ackup [CAP-DSM-07], recovery [CAP-DSM-04, QA-AVRL-01], and resilience [QA-A=
VRL-02].</strong></p>
<p>The platform aims to be extensible [QA-MAINT-01], maintainable [QA-MAINT=
-02], and portable [QA-PORT], providing a foundation for future data-driven=
 initiatives at eParts while mitigating vendor lock-in risks.</p>
<p>Please refer to the <a href=3D"https://epartsservices.atlassian.net/wiki=
/spaces/CMU2026/pages/818610498/Notional+Architecture" data-linked-resource=
-id=3D"818610498" data-linked-resource-version=3D"1" data-linked-resource-t=
ype=3D"page">Notional Architecture</a> for further details on the conceptua=
l model.</p>
<h3 id=3D"ePartsProductSpecificationDocument-4.2.High-LevelRequirements"><s=
trong>4.2. High-Level Requirements</strong></h3>
<p style=3D"margin-left: 30.0px;"><strong>4.2.1.</strong> The system shall =
support data ingestion from multiple sources within 5 seconds.</p>
<p style=3D"margin-left: 30.0px;"><strong>4.2.2.</strong> The system shall =
allow tenants to access only their own data.</p>
<p style=3D"margin-left: 30.0px;"><strong>4.2.3. </strong>The system shall =
provide a robust analytics dashboard.</p>
<p style=3D"margin-left: 30.0px;"><strong>4.2.4.</strong> The system shall =
provide an end-to-end MLOps platform that supports model training, versioni=
ng, and operational deployment.</p>
<p style=3D"margin-left: 30.0px;"><strong>4.2.5.</strong> The MLOps platfor=
m shall serve model predictions through a secure, tenant-aware API with per=
formance monitoring.</p>
<p style=3D"margin-left: 30.0px;"><strong>4.2.6.</strong> The system shall =
integrate with Elastic Search for writing data.</p>
<p><strong>Key Assumption:</strong> =E2=80=9CAll the requirements and desig=
ning is done assuming that all the tenant data can be aggregated together i=
n a single database=E2=80=9C</p>
<h2 id=3D"ePartsProductSpecificationDocument-5.UseCases"><strong>5. Use Cas=
es</strong></h2>
<p>(Derived primarily from April 1st 2025 Interviews, Persona documents (PS=
1-PS13) and Client Meetings)</p>
<h3 id=3D"ePartsProductSpecificationDocument-5.1.UC1"><strong>5.1. UC1</str=
ong></h3>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Global Tenant &amp; Usage Oversight (eParts Leadership/Admin - e.g., Leo=
 PS1, Jeb PS2, Diva PS3, Jade PS5):</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Goal: Understand overall platform health, tenant activity, sales trends,=
 and perform administrative actions across all tenants.</p></li>
<li>
<p>Scenario: Leo (COO) wants a dashboard showing key operational metrics ac=
ross all tenants. Jeb (CPO) needs to audit user activity logs [CAP-DSM-06] =
for a specific tenant. Diva (Architect) needs to manage RBAC roles [QA-SEC-=
01]. Leo wants to run a saved custom query [CAP-RA-08] showing product perf=
ormance trends and export the results to CSV [CAP-RA-09] for further analys=
is in Excel. He also wants this report scheduled monthly [CAP-RA-06].</p></=
li>
<li>
<p>Related Capabilities/Qualities: [CAP-RA-01], [CAP-RA-07], [CAP-DSM-06], =
[QA-USAB-01], [CAP-DAQ-01], [QA-SEC-01], [CAP-RA-08], [CAP-RA-09], [CAP-RA-=
06]</p></li>
</ul></li>
</ul>
<h3 id=3D"ePartsProductSpecificationDocument-5.2.UC2"><strong>5.2. UC2</str=
ong></h3>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Efficient PO Analysis &amp; Shipping Estimation (Tenant Data Manager / T=
enant Admin - e.g., Eddy PS8, Baron PS9):</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Goal: Reduce manual effort in aggregating purchase order data, get relia=
ble shipping cost estimates, and manage tenant-specific reporting.</p></li>
<li>
<p>Scenario: A Data Manager needs to analyze POs for his tenant, check hist=
orical price changes [CAP-DSM-02], and get shipping estimates. Eddy (Tenant=
 President) wants to execute a saved report template [CAP-RA-02] showing hi=
s tenant's monthly spending and export it to CSV [CAP-RA-09]. Baron (Tenant=
 Sales Mgr) needs to run an ad-hoc query [CAP-RA-03] on sales performance a=
nd manage user access for his team [CAP-DSM-05].</p></li>
<li>
<p>Related Capabilities/Qualities: [CAP-DI-05], [CAP-DSM-02], [CAP-RA-03], =
[CAP-RA-05], [QA-USAB-01], [CAP-RA-02], [CAP-RA-09], [CAP-DSM-05], [QA-SEC-=
01]</p></li>
</ul></li>
</ul>
<h3 id=3D"ePartsProductSpecificationDocument-5.3.UC3"><strong>5.3. UC3</str=
ong></h3>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Scoped Reporting &amp; Support (eParts Global User - e.g., Raine PS4, Dr=
ew PS6, Brock PS7 / Tenant User - e.g., Carlos PS10, Arnold PS11):</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Goal: Access specific data and reports relevant to assigned roles, proje=
cts, or tenants.</p></li>
<li>
<p>Scenario: Raine (Developer) needs access to logs [CAP-DSM-06] and query =
data [CAP-DAQ-01] for a specific tenant she's working on, but not others [Q=
A-SEC-01]. Drew (Support) needs to view standard dashboards [CAP-RA-01] for=
 a tenant to troubleshoot an issue. Brock (Sales) needs user analytics [CAP=
-RA-07] for his assigned tenants. Carlos (Tenant Acct Mgr) needs to run a s=
aved query [CAP-RA-08] showing sales history for his accounts and export to=
 CSV [CAP-RA-09]. Arnold (Tenant CSR) needs access to a subset of standard =
reports [CAP-RA-01].</p></li>
<li>
<p>Related Capabilities/Qualities: [CAP-DSM-01], [CAP-RA-03], [CAP-RA-05], =
[CAP-DAQ-01], [QA-SEC-01], [CAP-RA-01], [CAP-RA-07], [CAP-RA-08], [CAP-RA-0=
9]</p></li>
</ul></li>
</ul>
<h3 id=3D"ePartsProductSpecificationDocument-5.4.UC4"><strong>5.4. UC4</str=
ong></h3>
<ul>
<li>
<p>External BI Tool Integration (Tenant Analyst / Partner):</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Goal: Allow tenants or partners to analyze their permitted data using th=
eir preferred external Business Intelligence tools.</p></li>
<li>
<p>Scenario: A tenant analyst wants to connect their company's Power BI ins=
tance to the eParts data platform [CAP-DAQ-03] to create custom dashboards =
visualizing their order history. They authenticate via Auth0 [CON-01], acce=
ss only their tenant's data [QA-SEC-01], and expect reasonable query perfor=
mance. A partner like Siemens might use a similar API [CAP-DAQ-02] to pull =
agreed-upon aggregated data.</p></li>
<li>
<p>Related Capabilities/Qualities: [CAP-DAQ-03], [CAP-DAQ-04], [QA-SEC-01],=
 [CAP-DAQ-02]</p></li>
</ul></li>
</ul>
<h3 id=3D"ePartsProductSpecificationDocument-5.5.UC5"><strong>5.5. UC5</str=
ong></h3>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Near Real-Time Order Tracking (Customer Service - e.g., Jade PS5, Drew P=
S6):</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Goal: Quickly find and provide status updates for recent customer orders=
.</p></li>
<li>
<p>Scenario: A customer calls inquiring about an order. The support agent u=
ses a search interface to look up the order. The system returns the latest =
status reflected from near real-time CDC updates [CAP-DI-05, CAP-DAQ-05] wi=
thin 5 seconds.</p></li>
<li>
<p>Related Capabilities/Qualities: [CAP-DI-05], [CAP-DAQ-05]</p></li>
</ul></li>
</ul>
<h3 id=3D"ePartsProductSpecificationDocument-5.6.UC6"><strong>5.6. UC6 </st=
rong></h3>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Vendor Performance Monitoring (eParts Analyst):</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Goal: Track vendor reliability and data quality.</p></li>
<li>
<p>Scenario: An analyst reviews vendor metrics like document submission tim=
es [CAP-DI-10] and data accuracy. The system logs file receipts [CAP-DSM-06=
] and potentially flags vendors [CAP-DI-02]. This data might feed an ML ven=
dor scorecard.</p></li>
<li>
<p>Related Capabilities/Qualities: [CAP-DI-02], [CAP-DI-10], [CAP-DSM-06] (=
Ref: Feb 6-Logging, Flagging)</p></li>
</ul></li>
</ul>
<h3 id=3D"ePartsProductSpecificationDocument-5.7.UC7"><strong>5.7. UC7</str=
ong></h3>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Tenant Customer Reporting (Tenant Customer - e.g., Shawn PS12):</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Goal: Allow end-customers of tenants to access reports specific to their=
 own company's interactions.</p></li>
<li>
<p>Scenario: Shawn (Project Engineer at a tenant's customer) needs to run a=
 monthly report [CAP-RA-06] showing his company's order history for a speci=
fic product line. He needs access scoped only to his company's data within =
the tenant's environment [CAP-DSM-05]. He wants to save a custom query [CAP=
-RA-08] and export results to CSV [CAP-RA-09].</p></li>
<li>
<p>Related Capabilities/Qualities: [CAP-RA-01], [CAP-RA-06], [CAP-RA-08], [=
CAP-RA-09], [CAP-DSM-05], [QA-SEC-01]</p></li>
</ul></li>
</ul>
<h3 id=3D"ePartsProductSpecificationDocument-5.8.UC8"><strong>5.8. UC8</str=
ong></h3>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Online Inference &amp; Telemetry (Tenant-Facing App / eParts Backend =E2=
=80=93 e.g. Raine PS4):</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Goal<strong>:</strong> Serve low-latency, reliable predictions with live=
 health/performance visibility.</p></li>
<li>
<p>Scenario<strong>:</strong> The support app requests a shipping-time pred=
iction; the backend calls the inference endpoint [CAP-ML-06] via the MLOps =
API [CAP-DAQ-07]. The response includes prediction and model/version/stage.=
 Telemetry captures latency, errors, and data/target drift [CAP-ML-07]; ale=
rts surface on threshold breaches [QA-OBS-01]. Access is authenticated and =
tenant-scoped [QA-SEC-01].</p></li>
<li>
<p>Related Capabilities/Qualities: [CAP-ML-06], [CAP-ML-07], [CAP-DAQ-07], =
[QA-SEC-01], [QA-OBS-01]</p></li>
</ul></li>
</ul>
<h3 id=3D"ePartsProductSpecificationDocument-5.9.UC9"><strong>5.9. UC9 </st=
rong></h3>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Model Registry, Feature Store &amp; Promotion (eParts MLOps/Data Science=
 =E2=80=93 e.g., Raine PS4):</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Goal: Ensure governed, reproducible ML with safe rollout and rollback.</=
p></li>
<li>
<p>Scenario: Raine defines reusable features and publishes them to the feat=
ure store (online/offline) [CAP-ML-04] with lineage/artifact storage [CAP-D=
SM-10] and versioning [CAP-DSM-11]. A point-in-time training set is built [=
CAP-DSM-13], logged to experiment tracking [CAP-ML-05], and the trained mod=
el is registered [CAP-ML-03]; then reviews KPIs.</p></li>
<li>
<p>Related Capabilities/Qualities: [CAP-ML-03], [CAP-ML-04], [CAP-ML-05], [=
CAP-ML-08], [CAP-DAQ-07], [CAP-DSM-10], [CAP-DSM-11], [CAP-DSM-13], [QA-OBS=
-01], [QA-SEC-01]</p></li>
</ul></li>
</ul>
<h2 id=3D"ePartsProductSpecificationDocument-6.SystemCapabilities(Functiona=
lRequirements)"><strong>6. System Capabilities (Functional Requirements)</s=
trong></h2>
<h3 id=3D"ePartsProductSpecificationDocument-6.1.DataIngestion(CAP-DI)"><st=
rong>6.1. Data Ingestion (CAP-DI)</strong></h3>
<div class=3D"table-wrap">
<table data-table-width=3D"760" data-layout=3D"default" data-local-id=3D"44=
91925a-2f64-4842-a09e-a2cfe18664a8" class=3D"confluenceTable">
<colgroup>
<col style=3D"width: 144.0px;">
<col style=3D"width: 516.0px;">
<col style=3D"width: 98.0px;">
</colgroup>
<tbody>
<tr>
<th class=3D"confluenceTh">
<p><strong>Requirement ID</strong></p></th>
<th class=3D"confluenceTh">
<p><strong>Description</strong></p></th>
<th class=3D"confluenceTh">
<p><strong>Priority</strong></p></th>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>CAP-DI-01</strong></p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>The system shall ingest data from designated SQL Server databases (inclu=
ding source systems planned for migration to Azure SQL/Managed Instance). [=
CON-03]</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>MUST</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>CAP-DI-03</strong></p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>The system shall ingest data from various specified external feeds (e.g.=
, UPS shipping data). [CON-03]</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>MUST</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>CAP-DI-05</strong></p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>The system shall support Change Data Capture (CDC) streams from designat=
ed SQL Server tables for data synchronization. [UC2], [UC5]</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>MUST</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>CAP-DI-06</strong></p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>The system shall provide authorized operators the flexibility to trigger=
 specific ingestion processes on demand.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>MUST</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>CAP-DI-07</strong></p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>The system shall allow configuration to prioritize ingestion streams bas=
ed on data criticality or type (e.g., real-time vs. batch).</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>MUST</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>CAP-DI-08</strong></p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>The system shall provide a defined process to facilitate the integration=
 of new data sources in the future. [QA-MAINT-01]</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>MUST</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>CAP-DI-02</strong></p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>The system shall ingest files from Azure Blob Storage and SFTP locations=
, supporting formats including JSON, CSV, and text. [CON-03], [UC6]</p></td=
>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>SHOULD</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>CAP-DI-09</strong></p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>The system shall provide capabilities for transforming source data based=
 on defined schemas or mappings (e.g., via a mapping engine).</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>SHOULD</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>CAP-DI-04</strong></p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>The system shall ingest Application Performance Monitoring (APM) and app=
lication logging data from specified sources.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>COULD</p></td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</div>
<h3 id=3D"ePartsProductSpecificationDocument-6.2.DataStorage&amp;Management=
(CAP-DSM)"><strong>6.2. Data Storage &amp; Management (CAP-DSM)</strong></h=
3>
<div class=3D"table-wrap">
<table data-table-width=3D"760" data-layout=3D"default" data-local-id=3D"35=
a269c1-03a2-4ac6-b508-ee9c2fef9281" class=3D"confluenceTable">
<colgroup>
<col style=3D"width: 142.0px;">
<col style=3D"width: 526.0px;">
<col style=3D"width: 90.0px;">
</colgroup>
<tbody>
<tr>
<th class=3D"confluenceTh">
<p><strong>Requirement ID</strong></p></th>
<th class=3D"confluenceTh">
<p><strong>Description</strong></p></th>
<th class=3D"confluenceTh">
<p><strong>Priority</strong></p></th>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>CAP-DSM-01</strong></p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>The system shall store ingested and processed data in a centralized clou=
d-based data warehouse. [UC3]</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>MUST</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>CAP-DSM-02</strong></p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>The system shall provide mechanisms for storing and accessing historical=
 versions of data or data changes (e.g., through processed CDC streams or s=
napshotting). [UC2]</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>MUST</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>CAP-DSM-03</strong></p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>The system shall provide a secure mechanism for authorized personnel to =
delete specific customer or tenant data upon request, in compliance with pr=
ivacy regulations. [CON-06]</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>MUST</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>CAP-DSM-04</strong></p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>The system shall implement automated, regular (e.g., daily) data backup =
procedures, storing backups in a detached, secure location, and provide def=
ined data recovery capabilities aligned with RPO/RTO targets [QA-AVRL-01].<=
/p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>MUST</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>CAP-DSM-05</strong></p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>The system shall implement data governance policies, including role-base=
d access control (RBAC) integrated with Auth0 [CON-01], to enforce logical =
separation of tenant data [QA-SEC-01], allow administration of roles/permis=
sions within a tenant by Tenant Administrators [UC2, PS8, PS9], and support=
 data scoping to specific customer entities within a tenant where applicabl=
e [UC7, PS12]. [QA-SEC-01]</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>MUST</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>CAP-DSM-06</strong></p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>The system shall log activities performed by users (internal and potenti=
ally tenant/customer, where appropriate) within the data platform for audit=
 and monitoring purposes. [UC1], [UC6], [QA-SEC-01], [PS2, PS3, PS4, PS5]</=
p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>MUST</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>CAP-DSM-08</strong></p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>The system shall provide data in a normalized or structured form suitabl=
e for relational querying and BI tools where required. [QA-PORT-01]</p></td=
>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>MUST</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong> CAP-DSM-09</strong></p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>The system shall support the storage and querying of temporal data (data=
 valid over specific time periods).</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>MUST</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>CAP-DSM-07</strong></p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>The system shall allow data retention policies to be configured, potenti=
ally on a per-tenant or per-data-type basis.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>COULD</p></td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</div>
<h3 id=3D"ePartsProductSpecificationDocument-6.3.DataAccess&amp;Querying(CA=
P-DAQ)"><strong>6.3. Data Access &amp; Querying (CAP-DAQ)</strong></h3>
<div class=3D"table-wrap">
<table data-table-width=3D"760" data-layout=3D"default" data-local-id=3D"31=
9bb2b8-1ac4-4907-ace4-f65d431d5c3a" class=3D"confluenceTable">
<colgroup>
<col style=3D"width: 139.0px;">
<col style=3D"width: 527.0px;">
<col style=3D"width: 92.0px;">
</colgroup>
<tbody>
<tr>
<th class=3D"confluenceTh">
<p><strong>Requirement ID</strong></p></th>
<th class=3D"confluenceTh">
<p><strong>Description</strong></p></th>
<th class=3D"confluenceTh">
<p><strong>Priority</strong></p></th>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong> CAP-DAQ-01</strong></p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>The system shall allow authorized users (including Global Admins, scoped=
 Global Users, Tenant Admins, scoped Tenant Users, and scoped Tenant Custom=
ers) to execute queries against the data they are permitted to access, resp=
ecting defined governance policies [CAP-DSM-05]. [UC1], [UC3], [QA-SEC-01]<=
/p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>MUST</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>CAP-DAQ-02</strong></p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>The system shall provide documented APIs enabling authorized third-party=
 applications to retrieve processed data or analytics results.[UC4] [QA-INT=
-02]</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>MUST</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>CAP-DAQ-03</strong></p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>The system shall provide documented APIs specifically designed for integ=
ration with external Business Intelligence (BI) tools (e.g., Power BI, Tabl=
eau), using standard protocols where feasible [QA-PORT]. [UC4], [QA-INT-01]=
, [PS1, PS2, PS3, PS4, PS5, PS6, PS7, PS9] [CON-01]</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>MUST</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>CAP-DAQ-05</strong></p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>The search capability shall index data relevant for quick retrieval, spe=
cifically including shipment and order data. [UC5]</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>MUST</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>CAP-DAQ-06</strong></p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>The system shall support the creation and maintenance of denormalized da=
ta views specifically optimized for search performance (e.g., for catalog a=
nd order search).</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>MUST</p></td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</div>
<h3 id=3D"ePartsProductSpecificationDocument-6.4.Reporting&amp;Analytics(CA=
P-RA)"><strong>6.4. Reporting &amp; Analytics (CAP-RA)</strong></h3>
<div class=3D"table-wrap">
<table data-table-width=3D"760" data-layout=3D"default" data-local-id=3D"a0=
a4868d-57dd-482a-afe3-b26a31a57b2f" class=3D"confluenceTable">
<colgroup>
<col style=3D"width: 140.0px;">
<col style=3D"width: 523.0px;">
<col style=3D"width: 95.0px;">
</colgroup>
<tbody>
<tr>
<th class=3D"confluenceTh">
<p><strong>Requirement ID</strong></p></th>
<th class=3D"confluenceTh">
<p><strong>Description</strong></p></th>
<th class=3D"confluenceTh">
<p><strong>Priority</strong></p></th>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>CAP-RA-01</strong></p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>The system shall provide web-based dashboards for visualizing key metric=
s and exploring data, respecting user access permissions [CAP-DAQ-01, CAP-D=
SM-05]. [UC1], [UC3], [UC7], [PS1, PS2, PS3, PS5, PS6, PS7, PS8, PS9, PS10,=
 PS11, PS12]</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>MUST</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>CAP-RA-06</strong></p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>The system shall support scheduling the automatic generation and deliver=
y (e.g., via email) of predefined reports or saved queries [CAP-RA-08]. [UC=
1], [UC7], [PS1, PS6, PS7, PS12]</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>MUST</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>CAP-RA-07</strong></p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>The system shall support reporting and analytics on key business dimensi=
ons including, but not limited to, product performance, brand performance, =
order volumes, vendor interactions, system usage patterns (user analytics),=
 and login activity, respecting data access permissions [CAP-DAQ-01, CAP-DS=
M-05]. [UC1], [UC3], [PS1, PS2, PS3, PS4, PS5, PS7]</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>MUST</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>CAP-RA-08</strong></p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>The system shall allow report results and query results to be exported o=
r delivered in CSV format. [UC1], [UC2], [UC3], [UC7], [PS1, PS6, PS7, PS8,=
 PS9, PS10, PS12]</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>MUST</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>CAP-RA-02</strong></p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>The system shall allow authorized eParts users (e.g., Global Admins, cer=
tain Global Users) to create, manage, and deploy reusable report templates.=
 Tenant users shall be able to execute permitted templates. [UC2], [UC3], [=
UC7], [PS8, PS9, PS10, PS12]</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>SHOULD</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>CAP-RA-03</strong></p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>The system shall enable authorized users to generate and save ad-hoc rep=
orts based on the data they are permitted to access [CAP-DAQ-01, CAP-DSM-05=
]. [UC1], [UC2], [UC3], [PS1, PS2, PS3, PS4, PS5, PS6, PS7, PS9, PS12]</p><=
/td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>SHOULD</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>CAP-RA-04</strong></p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>The system architecture shall have a dedicated process for report delive=
ry (e.g., emailing). [QA-MAINT-02]</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>SHOULD</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>CAP-RA-05</strong></p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>The system shall provide a user interface, potentially including drag-an=
d-drop features, to facilitate report creation for users with varying techn=
ical skills. [UC2], [UC3], [QA-USAB-01]</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>SHOULD</p></td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</div>
<h3 id=3D"ePartsProductSpecificationDocument-6.5.MachineLearning(CAP-ML)"><=
strong>6.5. Machine Learning (CAP-ML)</strong></h3>
<div class=3D"table-wrap">
<table data-table-width=3D"760" data-layout=3D"default" data-local-id=3D"85=
599259-3a9b-4d83-8143-623fbb4ca6da" class=3D"confluenceTable">
<colgroup>
<col style=3D"width: 139.0px;">
<col style=3D"width: 525.0px;">
<col style=3D"width: 94.0px;">
</colgroup>
<tbody>
<tr>
<th class=3D"confluenceTh">
<p><strong>Requirement ID</strong></p></th>
<th class=3D"confluenceTh">
<p><strong>Description</strong></p></th>
<th class=3D"confluenceTh">
<p><strong>Priority</strong></p></th>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>CAP-ML-01</strong></p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>Cloud Resources:</strong> The platform shall provide managed com=
pute resources, object storage, and network isolation for all ML activities=
, including training, batch processing, and inference.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>MUST</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>CAP-ML-02</strong></p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>Feature Store &amp; ML Data Substrate:</strong> The platform sha=
ll implement open table formats (e.g., Delta Lake, Apache Iceberg, Apache H=
udi) to serve as the primary data substrate. This system must support versi=
oned datasets and features, data lineage tracking, and point-in-time reads =
for both online and offline feature serving.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>MUST</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>CAP-ML-03</strong></p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>Model Registry &amp; Versioning (MUST):</strong> The platform sh=
all provide a model registry. The registry must support model versioning, a=
pproval workflows, and maintain immutable links to the exact dataset and fe=
ature versions used for training. All experiment runs must be logged for re=
producibility.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>MUST</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>CAP-ML-04</strong></p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>Telemetry &amp; Monitoring (MUST):</strong> The platform must pr=
ovide key model performance indicators, including inference latency, error =
rates, and data or target drift. It must include a manual workflow for trig=
gering model retraining and promotion; automated retraining is explicitly d=
isallowed.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>MUST</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>CAP-ML-05</strong></p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>Data Quality Framework (MUST):</strong> The platform shall integ=
rate a data quality framework to define, execute, and monitor quality rules=
 on both source and transformed datasets.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>MUST</p></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>CAP-ML-06</strong></p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p><strong>Model Training for Shipping Time Estimation:</strong> The platfo=
rm could support the end-to-end training, validation, and deployment of a r=
egression model to predict shipping times.</p></td>
<td class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p>COULD</p></td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</div>
<h2 id=3D"ePartsProductSpecificationDocument-7.QualityAttributes(Non-Functi=
onalRequirements)"><strong>7. Quality Attributes (Non-Functional Requiremen=
ts)</strong></h2>
<p><strong>Note: </strong>For simplicity, we have removed the performance q=
uality attribute since the specific response times are yet to be finalized.=
</p>
<h3 id=3D"ePartsProductSpecificationDocument-7.1.Security(QA-SEC)"><strong>=
7.1. Security (QA-SEC) </strong></h3>
<p style=3D"margin-left: 30.0px;"><strong>7.1.1. QA-SEC-01:</strong> The sy=
stem shall provide role based access control(RBAC) to ensure tenant isolati=
on while querying data.</p>
<h3 id=3D"ePartsProductSpecificationDocument-7.2.Extensibility(QA-EXT)"><st=
rong>7.2. Extensibility (QA-EXT)</strong></h3>
<p style=3D"margin-left: 30.0px;"><strong>7.2.1. QA-EXT-01:</strong> The sy=
stem shall allow integration of new data sources for ingestion in the futur=
e.</p>
<p style=3D"margin-left: 30.0px;"><strong>7.2.2. QA-EXT-02: </strong>The te=
chnology stack shall minimize the number of disparate third-party vendors t=
o reduce integration complexity and simplify operational support within the=
 chosen cloud ecosystem.</p>
<h3 id=3D"ePartsProductSpecificationDocument-7.3.Usability(QA-USAB)"><stron=
g>7.3. Usability (QA-USAB)</strong></h3>
<p style=3D"margin-left: 30.0px;"><strong>7.3.1. QA-USAB-01: </strong>The s=
ystem shall allow users (both technical and non-technical) to access the re=
ports easily.</p>
<h3 id=3D"ePartsProductSpecificationDocument-7.4.Interoperability(QA-INT)">=
<strong>7.4. Interoperability (QA-INT)</strong></h3>
<p style=3D"margin-left: 30.0px;"><strong>7.4.1. QA-INT-01: </strong>The sy=
stem shall integrate with the existing eParts legacy systems and data sourc=
es.</p>
<p style=3D"margin-left: 30.0px;"><strong>7.4.2. QA-INT-02: </strong>The sy=
stem shall allow the use of multiple cloud service providers instead of a v=
endor lock in.</p>
<h3 id=3D"ePartsProductSpecificationDocument-7.5.Portability(QA-PORT)"><str=
ong>7.5. Portability (QA-PORT)</strong></h3>
<p style=3D"margin-left: 30.0px;"><strong>7.5.1. QA-PORT-01: </strong>The s=
ystem shall allow migration of core components (processing layer, ingestion=
 layer etc) in case of adversities.</p>
<h2 id=3D"ePartsProductSpecificationDocument-8.Constraints"><strong>8. Cons=
traints</strong></h2>
<p style=3D"margin-left: 30.0px;"><strong>8.1. CON-01:</strong> User authen=
tication and authorization for data access and governance capabilities shal=
l integrate with eParts' existing Auth0 implementation.</p>
<p style=3D"margin-left: 30.0px;"><strong>8.2. CON-02</strong>: The solutio=
n architecture must prioritize cost-effectiveness, specifically aiming to a=
void infrastructure costs that scale linearly per tenant where feasible (e.=
g., through shared resources for certain tiers or functions).</p>
<p style=3D"margin-left: 30.0px;"><strong>8.3. CON-03: </strong>The initial=
 set of primary data sources includes eParts' existing SQL Server (with a p=
lanned migration path towards Azure SQL Database or Managed Instance), Azur=
e Blob Storage, user-analytics sources, and specific external APIs/feeds li=
ke UPS.</p>
<p style=3D"margin-left: 30.0px;"><strong>8.4. CON-04: </strong>The initial=
 project implementation approach should favor breadth-first delivery (demon=
strating end-to-end functionality for a limited scope) over depth-first (fu=
lly building out one component).</p>
<p style=3D"margin-left: 30.0px;"><strong>8.5. CON-05: </strong>A formal ev=
aluation of potential core data platform technologies (including options li=
ke Azure Synapse, Azure Databricks, Microsoft Fabric, Snowflake, Confluent)=
 is required before final technology selection. This evaluation must consid=
er portability implications [QA-PORT-01]. [QA-MAINT-02]</p>
<p style=3D"margin-left: 30.0px;"><strong>8.6. CON-06:</strong> The system =
must provide mechanisms to comply with relevant data privacy regulations, i=
ncluding the ability to delete customer/tenant data upon request [CAP-DSM-0=
6].</p>
<p style=3D"margin-left: 30.0px;"><strong>8.6. CON-07:</strong> The ML capa=
bilities should be compatible with the existing Snowflake Data Lakehouse.</=
p>
<h2 id=3D"ePartsProductSpecificationDocument-9.OperationalScenarios"><stron=
g>9. Operational Scenarios</strong></h2>
<h3 id=3D"ePartsProductSpecificationDocument-9.1.OS-01:TenantBIReportingvia=
PowerBI"><strong>9.1. OS-01: Tenant BI Reporting via Power BI</strong></h3>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p>A Tenant Analyst [UC4] opens Power BI Desktop.</p></li>
<li>
<p>They use the eParts Data Platform connector/API endpoint [CAP-DAQ-03, QA=
-INT-01].</p></li>
<li>
<p>Authentication is handled via Auth0 redirect/credentials [CON-01, QA-SEC=
-01].</p></li>
<li>
<p>Power BI displays available datasets permitted for the authenticated ten=
ant user [CAP-DAQ-01, CAP-DSM-05].</p></li>
<li>
<p>The analyst selects the 'Sales Data' view and imports data for the last =
quarter. The API query responds.</p></li>
<li>
<p>The analyst builds visualizations and potentially exports underlying dat=
a to CSV [CAP-RA-09].</p></li>
</ol>
<h3 id=3D"ePartsProductSpecificationDocument-9.2.OS-02:SearchingforaRecentO=
rder(NearReal-Time)"><strong>9.2. OS-02: Searching for a Recent Order (Near=
 Real-Time)</strong></h3>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p>A Customer Service rep [UC5, PS5, PS6] receives an inquiry about a recen=
t order.</p></li>
<li>
<p>They use a global search bar in their CRM/Order Management tool, which q=
ueries the eParts Data Platform search API [CAP-DAQ-05].</p></li>
<li>
<p>The search API queries the search index [CAP-DAQ-05], respecting the rep=
's permissions [CAP-DSM-05], using data updated via CDC [CAP-DI-05].</p></l=
i>
<li>
<p>Matching order details are returned quickly and displayed to the rep.</p=
></li>
</ol>
<h3 id=3D"ePartsProductSpecificationDocument-9.3.OS-03:CreatingandUsingaSav=
edQuery"><strong>9.3. OS-03: Creating and Using a Saved Query</strong></h3>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p>An authorized eParts Global Admin (e.g., Leo PS1) logs into the Data Pla=
tform's reporting interface [CAP-RA-05].</p></li>
<li>
<p>They create a complex ad-hoc query [CAP-RA-03] to analyze cross-tenant p=
roduct adoption.</p></li>
<li>
<p>They save this query for future use [CAP-RA-08].</p></li>
<li>
<p>Later, they execute the saved query, retrieve the results, and export th=
em to CSV [CAP-RA-09]. They also schedule this query to run monthly [CAP-RA=
-06].</p></li>
</ol>
<h3 id=3D"ePartsProductSpecificationDocument-9.4.OS-04:RecoveringfromSimula=
tedDataLoss"><strong>9.4. OS-04: Recovering from Simulated Data Loss</stron=
g></h3>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p>During a planned test, an eParts IT Operator simulates the loss of the p=
rimary data warehouse storage.</p></li>
<li>
<p>The operator initiates the documented disaster recovery procedure [QA-AV=
RL-01].</p></li>
<li>
<p>The system restores data from the latest detached backup [CAP-DSM-04] to=
 a new instance.</p></li>
<li>
<p>The operator verifies data integrity and system functionality.</p></li>
<li>
<p>The total time taken (RTO) and the age of the restored data (RPO) are me=
asured against the defined objectives [QA-AVRL-01].</p></li>
</ol>
<h3 id=3D"ePartsProductSpecificationDocument-9.5.OS-05:ProcessingaVendorInv=
oicePDFviaSFTP"><strong>9.5. OS-05: Processing a Vendor Invoice PDF via SFT=
P</strong></h3>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p>A vendor uploads an invoice PDF to their designated SFTP folder.</p></li=
>
<li>
<p>The ingestion pipeline detects the new file [CAP-DI-02].</p></li>
<li>
<p>An OCR process extracts text and key fields from the PDF [CAP-DI-11].</p=
></li>
<li>
<p>A transformation step [CAP-DI-09] maps extracted fields to the standard =
data warehouse schema.</p></li>
<li>
<p>The processed invoice data is loaded into the data warehouse [CAP-DSM-01=
].</p></li>
<li>
<p>The ingestion process logs the successful receipt and processing of the =
file [CAP-DSM-06]. Potential data quality checks might flag issues [UC6].</=
p></li>
</ol>
<h3 id=3D"ePartsProductSpecificationDocument-9.6.OS-06:TenantCustomerAccess=
esOwnOrderHistory"><strong>9.6. OS-06: Tenant Customer Accesses Own Order H=
istory</strong></h3>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p>Shawn Miller (Tenant Customer) [UC7, PS12] logs into the tenant's storef=
ront portal which integrates with the Data Platform.</p></li>
<li>
<p>He navigates to a reporting section.</p></li>
<li>
<p>He executes a predefined report template [CAP-RA-02] showing his company=
's order history for the past 6 months. Access is scoped to only his compan=
y's data [CAP-DSM-05, QA-SEC-01].</p></li>
<li>
<p>He exports the report data to CSV [CAP-RA-09].</p></li>
</ol>
<h2 id=3D"ePartsProductSpecificationDocument-10.SystemOverview"><strong>10.=
 System Overview</strong></h2>
<p>Please refer to the <a class=3D"external-link" href=3D"https://miro.com/=
app/board/uXjVLi6rZcI=3D/" rel=3D"nofollow">WBS</a> and <a class=3D"externa=
l-link" href=3D"https://miro.com/app/board/uXjVLgBiP94=3D/" rel=3D"nofollow=
">Context Diagram</a>.</p>
<h2 id=3D"ePartsProductSpecificationDocument-11.Glossary"><strong>11. Gloss=
ary</strong></h2>
<p>11.1. Auth0: Identity and Access Management platform used by eParts for =
authentication and authorization. [CON-01]</p>
<p>11.2. BI: Business Intelligence. Technology-driven process for analyzing=
 data and presenting actionable information.</p>
<p>11.3. Blob Storage: Azure's object storage solution for unstructured dat=
a. [CON-03]</p>
<p>11.4. CDC: Change Data Capture. Process used to identify and capture cha=
nges made to data in a database. [CAP-DI-05]</p>
<p>11.5. Cloud-Agnostic: (In principle) The platform architecture is not fu=
ndamentally tied to a single cloud provider, although initial data sources =
and evaluation [CON-05] may favor one.</p>
<p>11.6. Data Warehouse: A central repository of integrated data from one o=
r more disparate sources, primarily used for reporting and analysis.</p>
<p>11.7. Elasticsearch: A distributed search and analytics engine.</p>
<p>11.8. ETL: Extract, Transform, Load. A type of data integration process.=
</p>
<p>11.9. KPI: Key Performance Indicator. A measurable value that demonstrat=
es how effectively a company is achieving key business objectives.</p>
<p>11.10. OCR: Optical Character Recognition. Technology that converts diff=
erent types of documents, such as scanned paper documents or image files, i=
nto editable and searchable data. [CAP-DI-11]</p>
<p>11.11. PO: Purchase Order.</p>
<p>11.12. POC: Proof of Concept. An initial small project to test the feasi=
bility of an idea or technology.</p>
<p>11.13. Power BI: Microsoft's interactive data visualization and business=
 intelligence tool. [UC4]</p>
<p>11.14. RBAC: Role-Based Access Control. A method of restricting system a=
ccess to authorized users based on their roles. [QA-SEC-01], [CAP-DSM-05]</=
p>
<p>11.15. RPO: Recovery Point Objective. The maximum acceptable amount of d=
ata loss measured in time (e.g., 1 hour of data). [QA-AVRL-01]</p>
<p>11.16. RTO: Recovery Time Objective. The targeted duration of time withi=
n which a business process must be restored after a disaster or disruption.=
 [QA-AVRL-01]</p>
<p></p>
    </div>
</body>
